{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NL5WiMo99m8rjK3Rzr24Dj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — nlp_variance_gtheory\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: AAAI 2027 (abstract Jul 21, paper Jul 28 — 9 weeks from today)\n5\t- Backup: ACL 2027 via ARR (October 15 cycle — 21 weeks)\n6\t- Extended: TACL (rolling)\n7\t\n8\t## Title\n9\tReproducibility Budgets for LLM Evaluation: Testing the Separability Assumption Between Infrastructure and Methodological Variance Sources via Generalizability Theory\n10\t\n11\t## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n12\t\n13\t**Claim 1 — Item Dominance**: Item selection is the single largest uncontrolled variance source in LLM evaluation, contributing more than prompt phrasing, random seed, temperature, numerical precision, and hardware type combined. (MVP evidence: item_id = 58.4% of total variance vs all other factors combined < 25%)\n14\t\n15\t**Claim 2 — Conditional Separability**: Infrastructure factors (hardware type, numerical precision) and methodology factors (prompt, seed, temperature, ordering) are approximately separable at the aggregate level (direct interaction < 0.5% of total variance), but both interact substantially with item difficulty — their effects are item-conditional, not universal. This provides an empirical license for isolated-factor studies while warning that their conclusions are conditional on item selection.\n16\t\n17\t**Claim 3 — Reproducibility Budget**: G-theory D-study projections yield quantitative reproducibility budgets showing that increasing item sampling is orders of magnitude more cost-effective than increasing prompt/seed replication for achieving reliable model comparisons (G ≥ 0.90). Current common practices (1 prompt, 1 seed, ≤200 items) produce G < 0.40.\n18\t\n19\t## Story Spine\n20\t\n21\t**Problem**: When LLM evaluation results vary across reproductions, practitioners cannot determine whether the culprit is prompt phrasing, random seed, GPU hardware, numerical precision, temperature, or item selection — let alone how these factors interact. Every prior study isolates at most two sources, implicitly assuming separability between infrastructure and methodology layers.\n22\t\n23\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Mesting (2026) applied G-theory to 5 methodological facets but treated infrastructure as fixed background. Yuan et al. (2025) documented up to 9% accuracy variation from hardware/precision but without factorial attribution. Brittlebench (2026) quantified prompt sensitivity at 50% variance but on fixed hardware. No study crosses both layers in a unified G-theory framework, and critically, no study has quantified the role of item selection relative to all other sources.\n24\t\n25\t**Our framing**: We conduct the first fully-crossed G-theory study spanning infrastructure (hardware type, numerical precision) × methodology (prompt, seed, temperature, ordering) × measurement (item) factors. The separability test has two equally publishable outcomes: if interactions are negligible, we grant an empirical license to isolated-factor studies; if substantial, we demonstrate that existing conclusions need hardware/prompt qualification. Our MVP reveals a third, unexpected finding: item selection dominates everything (58.4%), making it the overlooked key to evaluation reproducibility.\n26\t\n27\t**Headline result template**: \"In a fully-crossed G-study of K conditions across M models and N benchmarks, item selection accounts for >50% of total evaluation variance, while direct infrastructure × methodology interactions contribute <0.5%. Current evaluation practices achieve G < 0.40; our D-study reproducibility budgets show that tripling item count is 10× more effective than tripling prompt count for reaching G ≥ 0.90.\"\n28\t\n29\t## Hook (Counter-Intuitive Quantified Claim)\n30\t\"Researchers debating whether to standardize prompts, seeds, or GPU hardware for LLM evaluation are optimizing the wrong knobs — item selection alone accounts for 58% of total evaluation variance, more than all other factors combined.\"\n31\t\n32\t## Narrative Strategy\n33\t- **Type**: Cross-domain transfer (psychometrics G-theory → ML evaluation) + Breaking limitations (separability assumption challenge)\n34\t- **Tension**: \"Everyone's optimizing the wrong thing\" — the field focuses on prompt/seed/hardware standardization while ignoring item selection\n35\t- **Intro structure**: 4 paragraphs + 3 contributions (field mode from distilled writing patterns)\n36\t- **Signature visual**: Stacked-bar variance decomposition chart (field idiom from Mesting/Brittlebench)\n37\t- **Figure flow**: Problem illustration → G-theory facet diagram → Stacked-bar variance decomposition → D-study projection curves\n38\t\n39\t## Venue Fit Risks\n40\t- AAAI: Strong fit for \"evaluation methodology\" track. Risk: tight 9-week timeline requires overlapping experiments with writing.\n41\t- Reviewer concern 1: \"Only open-weight models, not API models\" — We intentionally study open-weight models where infrastructure is controllable; API models (studied by Mesting) have opaque infrastructure. Frame as complementary.\n42\t- Reviewer concern 2: \"G-theory is borrowed methodology, not novel\" — Frame as cross-domain transfer contribution. The novelty is the facet structure crossing infrastructure × methodology, not G-theory itself.\n43\t- Reviewer concern 3: \"Item dominance is obvious — harder items have more variance\" — Counter: (a) the magnitude (58%) was not previously quantified; (b) item×factor interactions (7% precision×item) are non-obvious; (c) the D-study implications for evaluation design are novel.\n44\t\n45\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n46\t1. **\"Only N GPU types\"** → exp-003 (multi-hardware crossing) addresses this\n47\t2. **\"float32 engine confound\"** → exp-001 fixes with consistent vLLM engine settings (V0 enforce_eager for all)\n48\t3. **\"Only MMLU\"** → exp-002 expands to GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag\n49\t4. **\"Small item sample\"** → exp-001 expands from 50 to 200 items\n50\t5. **\"No training-time analysis\"** → exp-006 (fine-tuning G-study with RoBERTa)\n51\t6. **\"Missing scale validation\"** → exp-005 (14B models)\n52\t7. **\"G-theory may not be right framework\"** → Compare with ANOVA and regression decomposition as sensitivity analysis\n53\t\n54\t## Design Decisions\n55\t- **Judge model fixed**: Unlike Mesting who includes judge as a facet, we fix the judge to isolate infrastructure × methodology interactions. Judge variance (Mesting: 43.8%) would dominate and obscure the effects we study. Adding judge is a natural extension for future work.\n56\t- **Generation-based evaluation**: Following Hua et al. (EMNLP 2025), we avoid log-likelihood scoring to eliminate scoring artifacts that inflate apparent prompt sensitivity.\n57\t- **Default vLLM settings**: We use default vLLM settings (without batch-invariant kernels) to reflect realistic practitioner conditions, making CUDA-level nondeterminism a measurable variance source.\n58\t- **vLLM 0.9.2**: Required for Blackwell GPU (sm_100/sm_120) + CUDA 12.8 support. Documented as hardware compatibility requirement.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4612c7a0-c8ae-42af-a27e-32f19ee90526","uuid":"9692e198-a1eb-472d-b646-a59f76059dad","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:21:03.820Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T190053/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — nlp_variance_gtheory\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: AAAI 2027 (abstract Jul 21, paper Jul 28 — 9 weeks from today)\n- Backup: ACL 2027 via ARR (October 15 cycle — 21 weeks)\n- Extended: TACL (rolling)\n\n## Title\nReproducibility Budgets for LLM Evaluation: Testing the Separability Assumption Between Infrastructure and Methodological Variance Sources via Generalizability Theory\n\n## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 — Item Dominance**: Item selection is the single largest uncontrolled variance source in LLM evaluation, contributing more than prompt phrasing, random seed, temperature, numerical precision, and hardware type combined. (MVP evidence: item_id = 58.4% of total variance vs all other factors combined < 25%)\n\n**Claim 2 — Conditional Separability**: Infrastructure factors (hardware type, numerical precision) and methodology factors (prompt, seed, temperature, ordering) are approximately separable at the aggregate level (direct interaction < 0.5% of total variance), but both interact substantially with item difficulty — their effects are item-conditional, not universal. This provides an empirical license for isolated-factor studies while warning that their conclusions are conditional on item selection.\n\n**Claim 3 — Reproducibility Budget**: G-theory D-study projections yield quantitative reproducibility budgets showing that increasing item sampling is orders of magnitude more cost-effective than increasing prompt/seed replication for achieving reliable model comparisons (G ≥ 0.90). Current common practices (1 prompt, 1 seed, ≤200 items) produce G < 0.40.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: When LLM evaluation results vary across reproductions, practitioners cannot determine whether the culprit is prompt phrasing, random seed, GPU hardware, numerical precision, temperature, or item selection — let alone how these factors interact. Every prior study isolates at most two sources, implicitly assuming separability between infrastructure and methodology layers.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Mesting (2026) applied G-theory to 5 methodological facets but treated infrastructure as fixed background. Yuan et al. (2025) documented up to 9% accuracy variation from hardware/precision but without factorial attribution. Brittlebench (2026) quantified prompt sensitivity at 50% variance but on fixed hardware. No study crosses both layers in a unified G-theory framework, and critically, no study has quantified the role of item selection relative to all other sources.\n\n**Our framing**: We conduct the first fully-crossed G-theory study spanning infrastructure (hardware type, numerical precision) × methodology (prompt, seed, temperature, ordering) × measurement (item) factors. The separability test has two equally publishable outcomes: if interactions are negligible, we grant an empirical license to isolated-factor studies; if substantial, we demonstrate that existing conclusions need hardware/prompt qualification. Our MVP reveals a third, unexpected finding: item selection dominates everything (58.4%), making it the overlooked key to evaluation reproducibility.\n\n**Headline result template**: \"In a fully-crossed G-study of K conditions across M models and N benchmarks, item selection accounts for >50% of total evaluation variance, while direct infrastructure × methodology interactions contribute <0.5%. Current evaluation practices achieve G < 0.40; our D-study reproducibility budgets show that tripling item count is 10× more effective than tripling prompt count for reaching G ≥ 0.90.\"\n\n## Hook (Counter-Intuitive Quantified Claim)\n\"Researchers debating whether to standardize prompts, seeds, or GPU hardware for LLM evaluation are optimizing the wrong knobs — item selection alone accounts for 58% of total evaluation variance, more than all other factors combined.\"\n\n## Narrative Strategy\n- **Type**: Cross-domain transfer (psychometrics G-theory → ML evaluation) + Breaking limitations (separability assumption challenge)\n- **Tension**: \"Everyone's optimizing the wrong thing\" — the field focuses on prompt/seed/hardware standardization while ignoring item selection\n- **Intro structure**: 4 paragraphs + 3 contributions (field mode from distilled writing patterns)\n- **Signature visual**: Stacked-bar variance decomposition chart (field idiom from Mesting/Brittlebench)\n- **Figure flow**: Problem illustration → G-theory facet diagram → Stacked-bar variance decomposition → D-study projection curves\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- AAAI: Strong fit for \"evaluation methodology\" track. Risk: tight 9-week timeline requires overlapping experiments with writing.\n- Reviewer concern 1: \"Only open-weight models, not API models\" — We intentionally study open-weight models where infrastructure is controllable; API models (studied by Mesting) have opaque infrastructure. Frame as complementary.\n- Reviewer concern 2: \"G-theory is borrowed methodology, not novel\" — Frame as cross-domain transfer contribution. The novelty is the facet structure crossing infrastructure × methodology, not G-theory itself.\n- Reviewer concern 3: \"Item dominance is obvious — harder items have more variance\" — Counter: (a) the magnitude (58%) was not previously quantified; (b) item×factor interactions (7% precision×item) are non-obvious; (c) the D-study implications for evaluation design are novel.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Planned Responses\n1. **\"Only N GPU types\"** → exp-003 (multi-hardware crossing) addresses this\n2. **\"float32 engine confound\"** → exp-001 fixes with consistent vLLM engine settings (V0 enforce_eager for all)\n3. **\"Only MMLU\"** → exp-002 expands to GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag\n4. **\"Small item sample\"** → exp-001 expands from 50 to 200 items\n5. **\"No training-time analysis\"** → exp-006 (fine-tuning G-study with RoBERTa)\n6. **\"Missing scale validation\"** → exp-005 (14B models)\n7. **\"G-theory may not be right framework\"** → Compare with ANOVA and regression decomposition as sensitivity analysis\n\n## Design Decisions\n- **Judge model fixed**: Unlike Mesting who includes judge as a facet, we fix the judge to isolate infrastructure × methodology interactions. Judge variance (Mesting: 43.8%) would dominate and obscure the effects we study. Adding judge is a natural extension for future work.\n- **Generation-based evaluation**: Following Hua et al. (EMNLP 2025), we avoid log-likelihood scoring to eliminate scoring artifacts that inflate apparent prompt sensitivity.\n- **Default vLLM settings**: We use default vLLM settings (without batch-invariant kernels) to reflect realistic practitioner conditions, making CUDA-level nondeterminism a measurable variance source.\n- **vLLM 0.9.2**: Required for Blackwell GPU (sm_100/sm_120) + CUDA 12.8 support. Documented as hardware compatibility requirement.\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01784f3ucxg1KUVbNm9VF7hb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Full-scale Precision Study (Confound Fixed)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"4 models × 3 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items, all using V0 enforce_eager\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_conditions\": \"1296_per_model\",\n7\t      \"total_records\": 1036800,\n8\t      \"item_id_variance_share\": 0.43,\n9\t      \"residual\": 0.21,\n10\t      \"precision_main_effect\": 0.008,\n11\t      \"precision_x_item\": 0.032,\n12\t      \"temperature_x_item\": 0.058,\n13\t      \"prompt_x_item\": 0.062,\n14\t      \"seed_x_item\": 0.024,\n15\t      \"ordering_main_effect\": 0.004,\n16\t      \"prompt_main_effect\": 0.012,\n17\t      \"temperature_main_effect\": 0.015,\n18\t      \"item_conditional_interactions_total\": 0.176,\n19\t      \"direct_infra_method_interaction\": 0.003,\n20\t      \"g_coefficient_current_practice\": 0.42,\n21\t      \"accuracy_bf16\": 0.681,\n22\t      \"accuracy_fp16\": 0.679,\n23\t      \"accuracy_fp32\": 0.674,\n24\t      \"model_agreement\": \"3 of 4 models show item_id as largest; Gemma-2 shows elevated prompt_x_item (~0.09) pulling item_id share to 0.36\"\n25\t    },\n26\t    \"tables\": [\n27\t      \"Table 1: Variance component estimates (% of total) by model — 4×12 matrix showing each component per model plus pooled\",\n28\t      \"Table 2: Accuracy means by precision level per model — confirms confound fix (三者差异<1pp vs MVP的8.5pp)\",\n29\t      \"Table 3: Model-level G coefficients under current practice conditions\"\n30\t    ],\n31\t    \"figures\": [],\n32\t    \"analysis\": \"Two-way ANOVA确认precision main effect在fix后从显著(p<0.001, η²=0.009)降为边际(p=0.03, η²=0.008)。Bootstrap CI for item_id share: [0.38, 0.48]。Gemma异常通过leave-one-model-out sensitivity analysis量化——移除Gemma后pooled item_id升至0.46。\\n\\n修复float32 confound后，MVP中precision=0.0087的main effect基本维持（因为BF16/FP16本身仍有差异），但precision×item从0.072骤降至0.032——MVP中float32使用了不同engine路径导致特定难题上的accuracy骤降，这部分interaction被消除。item_id纯方差从0.584降至0.43：原来的0.584中约有10-12pp是precision×item和temperature×item interaction在单一precision条件下被吸收进item主效应（50 items时估计不稳定）。200 items的stratified sampling提供更稳定估计，residual从0.176升至0.21反映了更大item pool中的unmodeled item×condition microvariance。Gemma-2-9B-IT因其instruction-tuning风格对prompt wording异常敏感（已知其system prompt格式要求严格），prompt×item interaction偏高，拉低了该模型的item_id相对份额。整体G=0.42仍然很低，验证了current practice不可靠的核心论点。\"\n33\t  },\n34\t  {\n35\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Benchmark Replication\",\n36\t    \"description\": \"4 models × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temps × 4 orderings on GSM8K/ARC-C/HellaSwag (200 items each)\",\n37\t    \"results\": {\n38\t      \"total_records_per_benchmark\": 230400,\n39\t      \"gsm8k_item_id_share\": 0.28,\n40\t      \"gsm8k_temperature_x_item\": 0.12,\n41\t      \"gsm8k_seed_x_item\": 0.08,\n42\t      \"gsm8k_residual\": 0.27,\n43\t      \"gsm8k_prompt_main\": 0.03,\n44\t      \"arc_challenge_item_id_share\": 0.38,\n45\t      \"arc_challenge_residual\": 0.22,\n46\t      \"arc_challenge_temperature_x_item\": 0.07,\n47\t      \"hellaswag_item_id_share\": 0.45,\n48\t      \"hellaswag_residual\": 0.19,\n49\t      \"hellaswag_prompt_x_item\": 0.05,\n50\t      \"cross_benchmark_item_dominance_as_largest\": \"3/4 benchmarks (GSM8K exception — residual+temp×item jointly exceed item_id)\",\n51\t      \"cross_benchmark_separability_holds\": \"3/4 benchmarks (direct infra×method < 0.02 everywhere)\",\n52\t      \"g_gsm8k_current\": 0.35,\n53\t      \"g_arc_current\": 0.4,\n54\t      \"g_hellaswag_current\": 0.48,\n55\t      \"replication_rate_item_as_single_largest\": 0.625\n56\t    },\n57\t    \"tables\": [\n58\t      \"Table 4: Cross-benchmark variance decomposition comparison — 4 benchmarks × top-8 components matrix\",\n59\t      \"Table 5: Benchmark characteristics (task type, answer format, difficulty distribution) vs variance structure mapping\"\n60\t    ],\n61\t    \"figures\": [],\n62\t    \"analysis\": \"Kruskal-Wallis test on per-item variance contributions across benchmarks confirms significant structural difference (H=47.3, p<0.001)。Permutation test for 'item_id is single largest component' yields replication probability 0.63 across random benchmark subsets。Key narrative shift: item dominance is benchmark-type-dependent, strongest for knowledge MC tasks, weaker for reasoning generation tasks。\\n\\nGSM8K是reasoning task，CoT generation引入大量stochastic variance——temperature直接影响推理链的分支选择，且不同seed下同一难题可能走完全不同的推理路径，导致temperature×item和seed×item interaction显著放大（合计0.20 vs MMLU的0.08）。residual也更高（0.27）因为generation过程本质上比MC selection更noisy。item_id仍有0.28但不再是单一最大源——residual(0.27)+temperature×item(0.12)合并后超过它。ARC-Challenge是science MC，结构更接近MMLU但题目难度分布更极端（容易题ceiling effect），item_id=0.38。HellaSwag最接近MMLU pattern（都是MC、都是knowledge/commonsense），item_id=0.45。跨benchmark的核心发现：MC benchmarks中item dominance稳健成立，但reasoning/generation benchmarks中variance structure根本不同——这本身成为novel finding。Separability在所有benchmark都成立（direct interaction<0.02），因为hardware/precision effects是low-level numerical的，与task type无关。\"\n63\t  },\n64\t  {\n65\t    \"name\": \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\",\n66\t    \"description\": \"4 models × 2 GPU types × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items\",\n67\t    \"results\": {\n68\t      \"hardware_status\": \"second GPU arrived late — only 2 models × reduced seeds(3) completed on GPU-2\",\n69\t      \"hardware_main_effect\": 0.012,\n70\t      \"hardware_x_precision\": 0.006,\n71\t      \"hardware_x_prompt\": 0.002,\n72\t      \"hardware_x_item\": 0.018,\n73\t      \"hardware_x_temperature\": 0.003,\n74\t      \"total_hardware_related_variance\": 0.041,\n75\t      \"direct_hardware_x_methodology_interaction\": 0.005,\n76\t      \"separability_conclusion\": \"holds at aggregate level — direct hardware×method < 1%\",\n77\t      \"item_id_with_hardware_facet\": 0.41,\n78\t      \"g_with_hardware_generalization\": 0.38,\n79\t      \"completeness\": \"partial — 2/4 models fully crossed, 2/4 models only on primary GPU\"\n80\t    },\n81\t    \"tables\": [\n82\t      \"Table 6: Hardware facet variance components (with CI) — noting which estimates are based on reduced crossing\",\n83\t      \"Table 7: Separability test — direct interaction terms between hardware and each methodology facet\"\n84\t    ],\n85\t    \"figures\": [],\n86\t    \"analysis\": \"Mixed-effects model with GPU as random effect confirms hardware contributes <2% unique variance。Acknowledge limitation: only 2 GPU types × partial model crossing — separability conclusion is directional, not definitive。Frame as 'consistent with separability' rather than 'proves separability'。计划在camera-ready前补充完整数据。\\n\\n第二块GPU延迟到达，只能对Qwen3-8B和Llama-3.1-8B做完整crossing（reduced seeds=3以控制时间）。Hardware main effect=0.012来自GPU间的kernel implementation差异（不同SM架构的floating-point rounding path不同），但远小于item_id。hardware×item=0.018表明特定难题在不同GPU上表现不同——这是因为numerical edge cases（接近decision boundary的logits）在不同GPU architecture上round differently。Direct hardware×methodology interaction仅0.005，验证separability——但这个结论基于incomplete crossing需要谨慎表述。数据不完整意味着hardware facet的估计CI较宽，论文中需作为limitation明确说明，但核心separability finding的方向性仍可支持。\"\n87\t  },\n88\t  {\n89\t    \"name\": \"D-Study Projections\",\n90\t    \"description\": \"Compute optimal measurement allocation from combined exp-001/002/003 variance components\",\n91\t    \"results\": {\n92\t      \"g_current_practice_mmlu\": 0.42,\n93\t      \"g_current_practice_gsm8k\": 0.35,\n94\t      \"g_current_practice_pooled\": 0.39,\n95\t      \"g_triple_items_mmlu\": 0.82,\n96\t      \"g_triple_prompts_mmlu\": 0.51,\n97\t      \"g_triple_seeds_mmlu\": 0.44,\n98\t      \"g_optimal_600items_mmlu\": 0.87,\n99\t      \"g_optimal_600items_3prompts_mmlu\": 0.91,\n100\t      \"items_needed_for_g90_mmlu\": 520,\n101\t      \"items_needed_for_g90_gsm8k\": 780,\n102\t      \"items_needed_for_g90_hellaswag\": 380,\n103\t      \"cost_ratio_items_vs_prompts_for_g90\": 3.8,\n104\t      \"cost_ratio_items_vs_seeds_for_g90\": 7.2,\n105\t      \"budget_table_achievable_g90\": \"600 items × 3 prompts × 2 seeds — feasible but 3× current practice\"\n106\t    },\n107\t    \"tables\": [\n108\t      \"Table 8: D-study projection matrix — rows=facet allocation scenarios, columns=benchmarks, cells=projected G\",\n109\t      \"Table 9: Practitioner budget table — 'to achieve G≥X on benchmark Y, sample at least Z items with W prompts'\",\n110\t      \"Table 10: Cost-effectiveness ratios — marginal G gain per additional level of each facet\"\n111\t    ],\n112\t    \"figures\": [],\n113\t    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity analysis: bootstrap resample variance components 1000×, compute D-study projections for each → 95% CI on 'items needed for G≥0.90' is [420, 680] for MMLU。Key message shift: 'tripling items is 3-5× more effective than tripling prompts' (down from '10×' in MVP)。仍然是strong practical recommendation但headline数字需要honest reporting。\\n\\nitem_id占比从MVP的58%降至MMLU的43%、跨benchmark均值约35%，导致D-study中tripling items的marginal gain缩小——从MVP预测的G提升0.35降至约0.25。具体来看：G(current)=0.42因为200 items在43% item variance下仍然欠采样（需要~520 items才能让item sampling error降到可接受水平）。Triple items(600)→G=0.82而非MVP外推的0.90+，因为residual(0.21)设定了ceiling——即使无限items，residual variance仍限制G上界约0.93。Triple prompts仅从0.42→0.51因为prompt-related variance(main+interactions)合计才~0.08，三倍prompt只压缩这小部分。Cost ratio从MVP的'10×'降至3.8×：items仍是最cost-effective lever但优势缩小。GSM8K需要更多items(780)因为其residual更高且item variance share更低——每增加一个item压缩的variance比例更小。这个'benchmark-dependent budget'本身成为实用贡献。\"\n114\t  },\n115\t  {\n116\t    \"name\": \"14B Model Extension\",\n117\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-14B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B at BF16/FP16 on MMLU 200 items\",\n118\t    \"results\": {\n119\t      \"qwen3_14b_item_id_share\": 0.46,\n120\t      \"deepseek_r1_14b_item_id_share\": 0.34,\n121\t      \"qwen3_14b_precision_main\": 0.005,\n122\t      \"deepseek_r1_precision_main\": 0.009,\n123\t      \"deepseek_r1_temperature_x_item\": 0.11,\n124\t      \"scale_effect_on_variance_structure\": \"mixed — dense 14B similar to 8B; reasoning-distilled shows more temperature sensitivity\",\n125\t      \"g_qwen3_14b_current\": 0.47,\n126\t      \"g_deepseek_r1_14b_current\": 0.38\n127\t    },\n128\t    \"tables\": [\n129\t      \"Table 11: 8B vs 14B variance component comparison — paired by architecture family\"\n130\t    ],\n131\t    \"figures\": [],\n132\t    \"analysis\": \"Key finding: variance structure is jointly determined by task type AND model architecture (specifically, reasoning-distilled models behave like 'reasoning tasks' even on MC benchmarks)。This adds nuance to the benchmark-dependent story。\\n\\nQwen3-14B作为dense model的scale-up版本，variance structure与8B系列相似但item_id略高(0.46)——更大模型对easy items更consistently correct，使item difficulty gradient更极端，增加item方差贡献。DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B是reasoning-distilled模型，其CoT倾向使temperature sensitivity大幅升高（temperature×item=0.11），类似GSM8K的pattern——即使在MC task(MMLU)上，该模型也倾向于'思考'，引入generation-like variance。这导致其item_id share仅0.34。这个发现支持'variance structure depends on model architecture, not just task type'的扩展论点。Precision main effect在两个14B模型上都很小（dense model更稳定），验证separability在larger scale也成立。\"\n133\t  },\n134\t  {\n135\t    \"name\": \"Fine-Tuning G-Study\",\n136\t    \"description\": \"RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA: 6 seeds × 3 LR × 4 shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task\",\n137\t    \"results\": {\n138\t      \"total_runs\": 1728,\n139\t      \"sst2_seed_variance_share\": 0.18,\n140\t      \"sst2_lr_variance_share\": 0.31,\n141\t      \"sst2_item_id_variance_share\": 0.22,\n142\t      \"sst2_shuffle_variance_share\": 0.04,\n143\t      \"sst2_gpu_variance_share\": 0.003,\n144\t      \"sst2_precision_variance_share\": 0.006,\n145\t      \"sst2_residual\": 0.15,\n146\t      \"sst2_seed_x_item\": 0.05,\n147\t      \"rte_seed_variance_share\": 0.28,\n148\t      \"rte_lr_variance_share\": 0.22,\n149\t      \"rte_item_id_variance_share\": 0.19,\n150\t      \"rte_seed_x_lr\": 0.08,\n151\t      \"copa_instability\": \"high residual (0.32) due to small dataset size\",\n152\t      \"g_finetuning_current_practice\": 0.52,\n153\t      \"g_finetuning_5seeds_3lr\": 0.78,\n154\t      \"infra_method_separability_finetuning\": \"holds — GPU×seed interaction < 0.5%\"\n155\t    },\n156\t    \"tables\": [\n157\t      \"Table 12: Fine-tuning variance decomposition — 4 tasks × top-8 components\",\n158\t      \"Table 13: Inference vs fine-tuning variance hierarchy comparison\",\n159\t      \"Table 14: Fine-tuning D-study — seeds and LR needed for G≥0.90\"\n160\t    ],\n161\t    \"figures\": [],\n162\t    \"analysis\": \"The inverted hierarchy (item→LR+seed) between inference and fine-tuning is a clean novel finding。It explains why the 'run 5 seeds and report mean±std' convention exists for fine-tuning but not for inference evaluation。Separability still holds in fine-tuning (GPU×methodology < 0.5%)，strengthening the cross-scenario generalization of Claim 2。\\n\\nFine-tuning的variance hierarchy与inference根本不同：learning rate成为dominant factor(SST-2上0.31)因为它决定了optimization trajectory的convergence point——不同LR到达不同local minima。Seed是第二大因素(0.18-0.28)因为weight initialization和data ordering jointly决定optimization path。Item_id仍significant(0.19-0.22)但不再dominant——fine-tuning使模型适配了task distribution，减少了item difficulty的极端效应。RTE上seed更重要(0.28)因为小数据集(2.5k training)使optimization对initialization更敏感。GPU variance几乎为零(0.003)因为fine-tuning的随机性远大于hardware-level numerical差异。Data shuffle仅0.04——远低于预期，因为在足够epochs后shuffle的影响被averaged out。核心对比：inference中item dominates(43%)，fine-tuning中LR+seed dominates(~50%)——practitioners需要不同的reproducibility strategies for不同scenarios。\"\n163\t  },\n164\t  {\n165\t    \"name\": \"LayerCast Precision Study\",\n166\t    \"description\": \"LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as 4th precision condition on MMLU\",\n167\t    \"results\": {\n168\t      \"layercast_accuracy\": 0.68,\n169\t      \"layercast_vs_fp32_accuracy_diff\": 0.006,\n170\t      \"layercast_vs_bf16_accuracy_diff\": -0.001,\n171\t      \"layercast_item_level_agreement_with_bf16\": 0.94,\n172\t      \"precision_variance_with_layercast\": 0.005,\n173\t      \"precision_x_item_with_layercast\": 0.022,\n174\t      \"variance_reduction_vs_mixed_precision\": \"15-20% reduction in precision-related variance components\"\n175\t    },\n176\t    \"tables\": [\n177\t      \"Table 15: 4-level precision comparison (FP32/BF16/FP16/LayerCast) — accuracy and variance metrics\"\n178\t    ],\n179\t    \"figures\": [],\n180\t    \"analysis\": \"LayerCast provides modest variance reduction but does not fundamentally change the story。Best framed as a practical recommendation in discussion: 'for practitioners concerned about precision effects, LayerCast offers ~18% reduction in precision-related variance at minimal memory cost'。\\n\\nLayerCast在FP16存储但FP32计算，理论上获得FP32的numerical stability同时保持FP16的memory efficiency。实测accuracy接近BF16/FP16（差异<0.1pp）而非接近pure FP32——这是因为在confound-fixed设置下FP32本身的accuracy已与BF16接近（差异<1pp），LayerCast的'storage in FP16'引入的quantization noise在compute阶段被FP32 accumulation部分补偿。Precision×item interaction从0.032降至0.022——LayerCast减少了precision-sensitive items上的variance但未完全消除（weight quantization仍在）。整体precision-related variance减少约18%，是有意义但非revolutionary的改进。作为mitigation strategy，值得在discussion中推荐但不足以成为standalone contribution。\"\n181\t  },\n182\t  {\n183\t    \"name\": \"MATH Benchmark Extension\",\n184\t    \"description\": \"MATH 200 items — reasoning-heavy with CoT, testing item dominance in extended generation\",\n185\t    \"results\": {\n186\t      \"math_item_id_share\": 0.22,\n187\t      \"math_temperature_main\": 0.04,\n188\t      \"math_temperature_x_item\": 0.15,\n189\t      \"math_seed_x_item\": 0.11,\n190\t      \"math_residual\": 0.3,\n191\t      \"math_prompt_x_item\": 0.06,\n192\t      \"math_precision_main\": 0.005,\n193\t      \"math_g_current\": 0.3,\n194\t      \"math_items_for_g90\": 950,\n195\t      \"item_dominance_holds\": false,\n196\t      \"separability_holds\": true\n197\t    },\n198\t    \"tables\": [\n199\t      \"Table 16: MATH vs GSM8K vs MMLU variance structure comparison — progression from MC to light-reasoning to heavy-reasoning\"\n200\t    ],\n201\t    \"figures\": [],\n202\t    \"analysis\": \"MATH completes the picture: variance structure is a continuous function of task reasoning demands。For MC knowledge tasks, item selection is the key lever; for reasoning tasks, temperature control and massive item sampling are both needed。The 'one-size-fits-all' reproducibility budget is insufficient — practitioners need task-type-specific guidance。This benchmark-dependency finding becomes the paper's central novel contribution under the median tier narrative。\\n\\nMATH是最极端的reasoning benchmark——每题需要多步推导，CoT generation在每一步都受temperature和seed影响。Temperature×item=0.15因为难题（Level 4-5）的solution path高度branching——temperature=0.7时可能走对路径，temperature=0.3时可能卡在suboptimal path。Seed×item=0.11同理——不同seed改变了sampling trajectory。Residual高达0.30反映了即使fixed所有facets，generation的intrinsic stochasticity（vLLM default设置下的CUDA nondeterminism在long generation中累积）。Item_id仅0.22——仍然是single largest individual component但margin很小（vs residual 0.30如果将residual视为'unexplained'则item不是最大）。这是median档下GSM8K pattern的加强版，确认了'reasoning tasks have fundamentally different variance structure'。Separability仍成立（precision/hardware与methodology无direct interaction>1%）——numerical precision不影响推理策略选择，只影响individual token probabilities。G=0.30极低，需要~950 items才能达到G≥0.90——对MATH这样仅500题的benchmark来说实质上不可达，这本身是对当前evaluation practice的strong critique。\"\n203\t  }\n204\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4612c7a0-c8ae-42af-a27e-32f19ee90526","uuid":"d51c1d9e-3d9d-49e1-8738-4a6543213029","timestamp":"2026-05-20T19:21:03.870Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T190053/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full-scale Precision Study (Confound Fixed)\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × 3 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items, all using V0 enforce_eager\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_conditions\": \"1296_per_model\",\n      \"total_records\": 1036800,\n      \"item_id_variance_share\": 0.43,\n      \"residual\": 0.21,\n      \"precision_main_effect\": 0.008,\n      \"precision_x_item\": 0.032,\n      \"temperature_x_item\": 0.058,\n      \"prompt_x_item\": 0.062,\n      \"seed_x_item\": 0.024,\n      \"ordering_main_effect\": 0.004,\n      \"prompt_main_effect\": 0.012,\n      \"temperature_main_effect\": 0.015,\n      \"item_conditional_interactions_total\": 0.176,\n      \"direct_infra_method_interaction\": 0.003,\n      \"g_coefficient_current_practice\": 0.42,\n      \"accuracy_bf16\": 0.681,\n      \"accuracy_fp16\": 0.679,\n      \"accuracy_fp32\": 0.674,\n      \"model_agreement\": \"3 of 4 models show item_id as largest; Gemma-2 shows elevated prompt_x_item (~0.09) pulling item_id share to 0.36\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Variance component estimates (% of total) by model — 4×12 matrix showing each component per model plus pooled\",\n      \"Table 2: Accuracy means by precision level per model — confirms confound fix (三者差异<1pp vs MVP的8.5pp)\",\n      \"Table 3: Model-level G coefficients under current practice conditions\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Two-way ANOVA确认precision main effect在fix后从显著(p<0.001, η²=0.009)降为边际(p=0.03, η²=0.008)。Bootstrap CI for item_id share: [0.38, 0.48]。Gemma异常通过leave-one-model-out sensitivity analysis量化——移除Gemma后pooled item_id升至0.46。\\n\\n修复float32 confound后，MVP中precision=0.0087的main effect基本维持（因为BF16/FP16本身仍有差异），但precision×item从0.072骤降至0.032——MVP中float32使用了不同engine路径导致特定难题上的accuracy骤降，这部分interaction被消除。item_id纯方差从0.584降至0.43：原来的0.584中约有10-12pp是precision×item和temperature×item interaction在单一precision条件下被吸收进item主效应（50 items时估计不稳定）。200 items的stratified sampling提供更稳定估计，residual从0.176升至0.21反映了更大item pool中的unmodeled item×condition microvariance。Gemma-2-9B-IT因其instruction-tuning风格对prompt wording异常敏感（已知其system prompt格式要求严格），prompt×item interaction偏高，拉低了该模型的item_id相对份额。整体G=0.42仍然很低，验证了current practice不可靠的核心论点。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Benchmark Replication\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temps × 4 orderings on GSM8K/ARC-C/HellaSwag (200 items each)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records_per_benchmark\": 230400,\n      \"gsm8k_item_id_share\": 0.28,\n      \"gsm8k_temperature_x_item\": 0.12,\n      \"gsm8k_seed_x_item\": 0.08,\n      \"gsm8k_residual\": 0.27,\n      \"gsm8k_prompt_main\": 0.03,\n      \"arc_challenge_item_id_share\": 0.38,\n      \"arc_challenge_residual\": 0.22,\n      \"arc_challenge_temperature_x_item\": 0.07,\n      \"hellaswag_item_id_share\": 0.45,\n      \"hellaswag_residual\": 0.19,\n      \"hellaswag_prompt_x_item\": 0.05,\n      \"cross_benchmark_item_dominance_as_largest\": \"3/4 benchmarks (GSM8K exception — residual+temp×item jointly exceed item_id)\",\n      \"cross_benchmark_separability_holds\": \"3/4 benchmarks (direct infra×method < 0.02 everywhere)\",\n      \"g_gsm8k_current\": 0.35,\n      \"g_arc_current\": 0.4,\n      \"g_hellaswag_current\": 0.48,\n      \"replication_rate_item_as_single_largest\": 0.625\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Cross-benchmark variance decomposition comparison — 4 benchmarks × top-8 components matrix\",\n      \"Table 5: Benchmark characteristics (task type, answer format, difficulty distribution) vs variance structure mapping\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Kruskal-Wallis test on per-item variance contributions across benchmarks confirms significant structural difference (H=47.3, p<0.001)。Permutation test for 'item_id is single largest component' yields replication probability 0.63 across random benchmark subsets。Key narrative shift: item dominance is benchmark-type-dependent, strongest for knowledge MC tasks, weaker for reasoning generation tasks。\\n\\nGSM8K是reasoning task，CoT generation引入大量stochastic variance——temperature直接影响推理链的分支选择，且不同seed下同一难题可能走完全不同的推理路径，导致temperature×item和seed×item interaction显著放大（合计0.20 vs MMLU的0.08）。residual也更高（0.27）因为generation过程本质上比MC selection更noisy。item_id仍有0.28但不再是单一最大源——residual(0.27)+temperature×item(0.12)合并后超过它。ARC-Challenge是science MC，结构更接近MMLU但题目难度分布更极端（容易题ceiling effect），item_id=0.38。HellaSwag最接近MMLU pattern（都是MC、都是knowledge/commonsense），item_id=0.45。跨benchmark的核心发现：MC benchmarks中item dominance稳健成立，但reasoning/generation benchmarks中variance structure根本不同——这本身成为novel finding。Separability在所有benchmark都成立（direct interaction<0.02），因为hardware/precision effects是low-level numerical的，与task type无关。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × 2 GPU types × 2 precisions × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hardware_status\": \"second GPU arrived late — only 2 models × reduced seeds(3) completed on GPU-2\",\n      \"hardware_main_effect\": 0.012,\n      \"hardware_x_precision\": 0.006,\n      \"hardware_x_prompt\": 0.002,\n      \"hardware_x_item\": 0.018,\n      \"hardware_x_temperature\": 0.003,\n      \"total_hardware_related_variance\": 0.041,\n      \"direct_hardware_x_methodology_interaction\": 0.005,\n      \"separability_conclusion\": \"holds at aggregate level — direct hardware×method < 1%\",\n      \"item_id_with_hardware_facet\": 0.41,\n      \"g_with_hardware_generalization\": 0.38,\n      \"completeness\": \"partial — 2/4 models fully crossed, 2/4 models only on primary GPU\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: Hardware facet variance components (with CI) — noting which estimates are based on reduced crossing\",\n      \"Table 7: Separability test — direct interaction terms between hardware and each methodology facet\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mixed-effects model with GPU as random effect confirms hardware contributes <2% unique variance。Acknowledge limitation: only 2 GPU types × partial model crossing — separability conclusion is directional, not definitive。Frame as 'consistent with separability' rather than 'proves separability'。计划在camera-ready前补充完整数据。\\n\\n第二块GPU延迟到达，只能对Qwen3-8B和Llama-3.1-8B做完整crossing（reduced seeds=3以控制时间）。Hardware main effect=0.012来自GPU间的kernel implementation差异（不同SM架构的floating-point rounding path不同），但远小于item_id。hardware×item=0.018表明特定难题在不同GPU上表现不同——这是因为numerical edge cases（接近decision boundary的logits）在不同GPU architecture上round differently。Direct hardware×methodology interaction仅0.005，验证separability——但这个结论基于incomplete crossing需要谨慎表述。数据不完整意味着hardware facet的估计CI较宽，论文中需作为limitation明确说明，但核心separability finding的方向性仍可支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"D-Study Projections\",\n    \"description\": \"Compute optimal measurement allocation from combined exp-001/002/003 variance components\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"g_current_practice_mmlu\": 0.42,\n      \"g_current_practice_gsm8k\": 0.35,\n      \"g_current_practice_pooled\": 0.39,\n      \"g_triple_items_mmlu\": 0.82,\n      \"g_triple_prompts_mmlu\": 0.51,\n      \"g_triple_seeds_mmlu\": 0.44,\n      \"g_optimal_600items_mmlu\": 0.87,\n      \"g_optimal_600items_3prompts_mmlu\": 0.91,\n      \"items_needed_for_g90_mmlu\": 520,\n      \"items_needed_for_g90_gsm8k\": 780,\n      \"items_needed_for_g90_hellaswag\": 380,\n      \"cost_ratio_items_vs_prompts_for_g90\": 3.8,\n      \"cost_ratio_items_vs_seeds_for_g90\": 7.2,\n      \"budget_table_achievable_g90\": \"600 items × 3 prompts × 2 seeds — feasible but 3× current practice\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: D-study projection matrix — rows=facet allocation scenarios, columns=benchmarks, cells=projected G\",\n      \"Table 9: Practitioner budget table — 'to achieve G≥X on benchmark Y, sample at least Z items with W prompts'\",\n      \"Table 10: Cost-effectiveness ratios — marginal G gain per additional level of each facet\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sensitivity analysis: bootstrap resample variance components 1000×, compute D-study projections for each → 95% CI on 'items needed for G≥0.90' is [420, 680] for MMLU。Key message shift: 'tripling items is 3-5× more effective than tripling prompts' (down from '10×' in MVP)。仍然是strong practical recommendation但headline数字需要honest reporting。\\n\\nitem_id占比从MVP的58%降至MMLU的43%、跨benchmark均值约35%，导致D-study中tripling items的marginal gain缩小——从MVP预测的G提升0.35降至约0.25。具体来看：G(current)=0.42因为200 items在43% item variance下仍然欠采样（需要~520 items才能让item sampling error降到可接受水平）。Triple items(600)→G=0.82而非MVP外推的0.90+，因为residual(0.21)设定了ceiling——即使无限items，residual variance仍限制G上界约0.93。Triple prompts仅从0.42→0.51因为prompt-related variance(main+interactions)合计才~0.08，三倍prompt只压缩这小部分。Cost ratio从MVP的'10×'降至3.8×：items仍是最cost-effective lever但优势缩小。GSM8K需要更多items(780)因为其residual更高且item variance share更低——每增加一个item压缩的variance比例更小。这个'benchmark-dependent budget'本身成为实用贡献。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"14B Model Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-14B and DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B at BF16/FP16 on MMLU 200 items\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"qwen3_14b_item_id_share\": 0.46,\n      \"deepseek_r1_14b_item_id_share\": 0.34,\n      \"qwen3_14b_precision_main\": 0.005,\n      \"deepseek_r1_precision_main\": 0.009,\n      \"deepseek_r1_temperature_x_item\": 0.11,\n      \"scale_effect_on_variance_structure\": \"mixed — dense 14B similar to 8B; reasoning-distilled shows more temperature sensitivity\",\n      \"g_qwen3_14b_current\": 0.47,\n      \"g_deepseek_r1_14b_current\": 0.38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 11: 8B vs 14B variance component comparison — paired by architecture family\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Key finding: variance structure is jointly determined by task type AND model architecture (specifically, reasoning-distilled models behave like 'reasoning tasks' even on MC benchmarks)。This adds nuance to the benchmark-dependent story。\\n\\nQwen3-14B作为dense model的scale-up版本，variance structure与8B系列相似但item_id略高(0.46)——更大模型对easy items更consistently correct，使item difficulty gradient更极端，增加item方差贡献。DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B是reasoning-distilled模型，其CoT倾向使temperature sensitivity大幅升高（temperature×item=0.11），类似GSM8K的pattern——即使在MC task(MMLU)上，该模型也倾向于'思考'，引入generation-like variance。这导致其item_id share仅0.34。这个发现支持'variance structure depends on model architecture, not just task type'的扩展论点。Precision main effect在两个14B模型上都很小（dense model更稳定），验证separability在larger scale也成立。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Fine-Tuning G-Study\",\n    \"description\": \"RoBERTa-large on SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA: 6 seeds × 3 LR × 4 shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_runs\": 1728,\n      \"sst2_seed_variance_share\": 0.18,\n      \"sst2_lr_variance_share\": 0.31,\n      \"sst2_item_id_variance_share\": 0.22,\n      \"sst2_shuffle_variance_share\": 0.04,\n      \"sst2_gpu_variance_share\": 0.003,\n      \"sst2_precision_variance_share\": 0.006,\n      \"sst2_residual\": 0.15,\n      \"sst2_seed_x_item\": 0.05,\n      \"rte_seed_variance_share\": 0.28,\n      \"rte_lr_variance_share\": 0.22,\n      \"rte_item_id_variance_share\": 0.19,\n      \"rte_seed_x_lr\": 0.08,\n      \"copa_instability\": \"high residual (0.32) due to small dataset size\",\n      \"g_finetuning_current_practice\": 0.52,\n      \"g_finetuning_5seeds_3lr\": 0.78,\n      \"infra_method_separability_finetuning\": \"holds — GPU×seed interaction < 0.5%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 12: Fine-tuning variance decomposition — 4 tasks × top-8 components\",\n      \"Table 13: Inference vs fine-tuning variance hierarchy comparison\",\n      \"Table 14: Fine-tuning D-study — seeds and LR needed for G≥0.90\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"The inverted hierarchy (item→LR+seed) between inference and fine-tuning is a clean novel finding。It explains why the 'run 5 seeds and report mean±std' convention exists for fine-tuning but not for inference evaluation。Separability still holds in fine-tuning (GPU×methodology < 0.5%)，strengthening the cross-scenario generalization of Claim 2。\\n\\nFine-tuning的variance hierarchy与inference根本不同：learning rate成为dominant factor(SST-2上0.31)因为它决定了optimization trajectory的convergence point——不同LR到达不同local minima。Seed是第二大因素(0.18-0.28)因为weight initialization和data ordering jointly决定optimization path。Item_id仍significant(0.19-0.22)但不再dominant——fine-tuning使模型适配了task distribution，减少了item difficulty的极端效应。RTE上seed更重要(0.28)因为小数据集(2.5k training)使optimization对initialization更敏感。GPU variance几乎为零(0.003)因为fine-tuning的随机性远大于hardware-level numerical差异。Data shuffle仅0.04——远低于预期，因为在足够epochs后shuffle的影响被averaged out。核心对比：inference中item dominates(43%)，fine-tuning中LR+seed dominates(~50%)——practitioners需要不同的reproducibility strategies for不同scenarios。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LayerCast Precision Study\",\n    \"description\": \"LayerCast (FP16 storage + FP32 compute) as 4th precision condition on MMLU\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"layercast_accuracy\": 0.68,\n      \"layercast_vs_fp32_accuracy_diff\": 0.006,\n      \"layercast_vs_bf16_accuracy_diff\": -0.001,\n      \"layercast_item_level_agreement_with_bf16\": 0.94,\n      \"precision_variance_with_layercast\": 0.005,\n      \"precision_x_item_with_layercast\": 0.022,\n      \"variance_reduction_vs_mixed_precision\": \"15-20% reduction in precision-related variance components\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 15: 4-level precision comparison (FP32/BF16/FP16/LayerCast) — accuracy and variance metrics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LayerCast provides modest variance reduction but does not fundamentally change the story。Best framed as a practical recommendation in discussion: 'for practitioners concerned about precision effects, LayerCast offers ~18% reduction in precision-related variance at minimal memory cost'。\\n\\nLayerCast在FP16存储但FP32计算，理论上获得FP32的numerical stability同时保持FP16的memory efficiency。实测accuracy接近BF16/FP16（差异<0.1pp）而非接近pure FP32——这是因为在confound-fixed设置下FP32本身的accuracy已与BF16接近（差异<1pp），LayerCast的'storage in FP16'引入的quantization noise在compute阶段被FP32 accumulation部分补偿。Precision×item interaction从0.032降至0.022——LayerCast减少了precision-sensitive items上的variance但未完全消除（weight quantization仍在）。整体precision-related variance减少约18%，是有意义但非revolutionary的改进。作为mitigation strategy，值得在discussion中推荐但不足以成为standalone contribution。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MATH Benchmark Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"MATH 200 items — reasoning-heavy with CoT, testing item dominance in extended generation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"math_item_id_share\": 0.22,\n      \"math_temperature_main\": 0.04,\n      \"math_temperature_x_item\": 0.15,\n      \"math_seed_x_item\": 0.11,\n      \"math_residual\": 0.3,\n      \"math_prompt_x_item\": 0.06,\n      \"math_precision_main\": 0.005,\n      \"math_g_current\": 0.3,\n      \"math_items_for_g90\": 950,\n      \"item_dominance_holds\": false,\n      \"separability_holds\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 16: MATH vs GSM8K vs MMLU variance structure comparison — progression from MC to light-reasoning to heavy-reasoning\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"MATH completes the picture: variance structure is a continuous function of task reasoning demands。For MC knowledge tasks, item selection is the key lever; for reasoning tasks, temperature control and massive item sampling are both needed。The 'one-size-fits-all' reproducibility budget is insufficient — practitioners need task-type-specific guidance。This benchmark-dependency finding becomes the paper's central novel contribution under the median tier narrative。\\n\\nMATH是最极端的reasoning benchmark——每题需要多步推导，CoT generation在每一步都受temperature和seed影响。Temperature×item=0.15因为难题（Level 4-5）的solution path高度branching——temperature=0.7时可能走对路径，temperature=0.3时可能卡在suboptimal path。Seed×item=0.11同理——不同seed改变了sampling trajectory。Residual高达0.30反映了即使fixed所有facets，generation的intrinsic stochasticity（vLLM default设置下的CUDA nondeterminism在long generation中累积）。Item_id仅0.22——仍然是single largest individual component但margin很小（vs residual 0.30如果将residual视为'unexplained'则item不是最大）。这是median档下GSM8K pattern的加强版，确认了'reasoning tasks have fundamentally different variance structure'。Separability仍成立（precision/hardware与methodology无direct interaction>1%）——numerical precision不影响推理策略选择，只影响individual token probabilities。G=0.30极低，需要~950 items才能达到G≥0.90——对MATH这样仅500题的benchmark来说实质上不可达，这本身是对当前evaluation practice的strong critique。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
