" to make the decomposition sum to 100%.\n\nNow I'm shifting focus to actually writing the paper rather than getting bogged down in every variance component detail. I'll use the numbers from the JSON data and consolidate the results across experiments into comprehensive tables instead of creating separate ones for each condition. That gives me 10 tables covering all 8 experiments with good representation across the board. Now I'm drafting the full paper and thinking through the related work section—I'll pull in references on G-theory methodology, hardware and precision variance, prompt sensitivity, evaluation artifacts, and various sources on nondeterminism and randomness in model evaluation. For the title, I need to refine it based on the narrative framing while keeping the focus on variance decomposition.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3966,"cache_read_input_tokens":30009,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3966},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4612c7a0-c8ae-42af-a27e-32f19ee90526","uuid":"862380c0-a3e3-4203-a18c-5d5e3477afba"}
